.Dd $Mdocdate: April 18 2026 $
.Dt BTD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm btd
.Nd Bluetooth daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dnv
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
drives a USB Bluetooth controller attached as
.Xr ugen 4
from userland.
It keeps Bluetooth Low Energy keyboards and mice connected and feeds
their input into
.Xr wscons 4 ,
and plays the
.Xr sndiod 8
mix on an A2DP headset, with the headset volume tied to the
.Va output.level
control.
.Pp
Without a
.Ic device
in
.Xr btd.conf 5 ,
the first Bluetooth controller found on any USB bus is used.
Realtek RTL8761BU controllers get their firmware loaded from
.Pa /etc/firmware .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Do not daemonize.
If this option is specified,
.Nm
will run in the foreground and log to
.Em stderr .
.It Fl f Ar file
Specify an alternative configuration file.
.It Fl n
Configtest mode.
Only check the configuration file for validity.
With
.Fl v ,
also print the parsed configuration.
.It Fl s Ar socket
Use an alternate location for the default control socket.
.It Fl v
Produce more verbose output.
Multiple
.Fl v
options increase the verbosity; three of them trace every HCI packet.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
runs as several processes.
The main process reads the configuration, the firmware and the bonds
and stores new bonds.
The bus process moves HCI packets between the controller and the
engine and injects input events; it holds the device nodes and runs
without
.Xr pledge 2 ,
restricted by
.Xr unveil 2 .
A child of it blocks reading the bulk endpoint.
The engine process, chrooted and pledged to
.Dq stdio ,
parses everything that comes from the radio: HCI, L2CAP, pairing,
GATT, HID, SDP, AVDTP and AVRCP.
The frontend process serves the control socket and talks to
.Xr sndiod 8 :
it records the monitor sub-device and encodes it to SBC.
.Sh PAIRING
A device listed in
.Xr btd.conf 5
that is not bonded yet is paired when it is found.
LE devices use Secure Connections; a keyboard asks for a six digit
passkey, which
.Nm
logs and
.Xr btctl 8
shows: type it on the keyboard and press Enter.
Headsets pair with Secure Simple Pairing, Just Works.
Every link must be encrypted with a 16 octet key;
a device that offers a shorter one is refused.
Put the device in pairing mode before starting
.Nm
or reloading its configuration.
.Pp
A bond is never replaced on the device's initiative.
If a bonded device no longer has the key, for example after pairing
with another host, the link fails and
.Nm
logs it.
Remove the bond with the
.Cm unpair
command of
.Xr btctl 8
to pair it again.
.Sh AUDIO
.Xr sndiod 8
needs a monitor-only sub-device at the SBC rate, for example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sndiod_flags="-r 48000 -z 480 -b 1920 -s default -m mon -s mon"
.Ed
.Pp
The frontend connects to
.Xr sndiod 8
as
.Dq _btd
and must present the session cookie of the user owning the server:
copy
.Pa ~/.sndio/cookie
of that user to
.Pa /var/db/btd/.sndio/cookie ,
owned by
.Dq _btd
with mode 0600.
.Sh HOTPLUG
When the controller is removed,
.Nm
exits.
It can be restarted when the controller comes back from
.Pa /etc/hotplug/attach :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
case $1 in
0)	case $2 in
	ugen*)	rcctl restart btd ;;
	esac ;;
esac
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/db/btd/.sndio/cookieXX" -compact
.It Pa /etc/btd.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /dev/btd.sock
.Ux Ns -domain
socket used for communication with
.Xr btctl 8 .
.It Pa /var/db/btd/bonds
Keys of paired devices and the local identity.
.It Pa /var/db/btd/.sndio/cookie
.Xr sndiod 8
session cookie.
.It Pa /etc/firmware/rtl8761bu_fw
.It Pa /etc/firmware/rtl8761bu_config
RTL8761BU firmware and configuration.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ugen 4 ,
.Xr wscons 4 ,
.Xr btd.conf 5 ,
.Xr btctl 8 ,
.Xr sndiod 8
.Sh CAVEATS
Injected input reaches the
.Xr wscons 4
multiplexers, that is X and any other mux reader, but not the text
console.
